{
 "id": "prefix-1",
 "part": "Β",
 "el": "Προθήματα από προθέσεις (Α)",
 "title": "Prepositional prefixes I: ανα-, απο-, δια-, εκ-/εξ-, εν-",
 "level": "A2–C1",
 "intro": [
  {
   "p": "Most Greek prefixes are old prepositions. Each has a basic spatial sense (up, away, through, out, in) and a few figurative ones that grew from it. Learn the spatial sense first and the figurative ones follow."
  },
  {
   "tip": "Prefixes ending in a vowel usually drop it before a vowel (**απο- + ουσία** → **απουσία**, **κατα- + οικώ** → **κατοικώ**). Before a vowel that once had a rough breathing they also turn π and τ into φ and θ (**απο- + αιρώ** → **αφαιρώ**, **μετα- + αύριο** → **μεθαύριο**, **κατα- + ιερός** → **καθιερώνω**). The breathing is no longer written, so learn these as they come. **περι-** and **προ-** never drop their vowel."
  }
 ],
